&gt; ⇄  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">Connect</span></span><span> this directory </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">to</span></span><span> an existing Netlify project
  +  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">Create</span></span><span> &amp; configure a </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">new</span></span><span> project
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
<ol data-start="190" data-end="1018">
<li data-start="190" data-end="326">
<p data-start="193" data-end="326"><strong data-start="193" data-end="217">Use your ↓ arrow key</strong> to make sure “Connect this directory to an existing Netlify project” is highlighted, then <strong data-start="308" data-end="323">press Enter</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="327" data-end="490">
<p data-start="330" data-end="490">You’ll get a list of your Netlify sites — use the ↑/↓ arrows to find your Townsend site (it’ll look like “same‑k9b4q7zbb4s” or similar), then <strong data-start="472" data-end="487">press Enter</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="491" data-end="622">
<p data-start="494" data-end="509">When prompted</p>
