31 15.3408L9.2168 15.2305C9.36965 15.1046 9.55583 14.9207 9.90527 14.5713L14.8926 9.58301L11.666 6.35742L6.67871 11.3447ZM16.1963 5.05371C15.3054 4.16304 13.8616 4.16305 12.9707 5.05371L12.6074 5.41602L15.833 8.64258L16.1963 8.2793C17.0869 7.38845 17.0869 5.94456 16.1963 5.05371Z"></path><path d="M4.58301 1.7832C4.72589 1.7832 4.84877 1.88437 4.87695 2.02441C4.99384 2.60873 5.22432 3.11642 5.58398 3.50391C5.94115 3.88854 6.44253 4.172 7.13281 4.28711C7.27713 4.3114 7.38267 4.43665 7.38281 4.58301C7.38281 4.7295 7.27723 4.8546 7.13281 4.87891C6.44249 4.99401 5.94116 5.27746 5.58398 5.66211C5.26908 6.00126 5.05404 6.43267 4.92676 6.92676L4.87695 7.1416C4.84891 7.28183 4.72601 7.38281 4.58301 7.38281C4.44013 7.38267 4.31709 7.28173 4.28906 7.1416C4.17212 6.55728 3.94179 6.04956 3.58203 5.66211C3.22483 5.27757 2.72347 4.99395 2.0332 4.87891C1.88897 4.85446 1.7832 4.72938 1.7832 4.58301C1.78335 4.43673 1.88902 4.3115 2.0332 4.28711C2.72366 4.17203 3.22481 3.88861 3.58203 3.50391C3.94186 3.11638 4.17214 2.60888 4.28906 2.02441L4.30371 1.97363C4.34801 1.86052 4.45804 1.78333 4.58301 1.7832Z"></path></svg>Edit</button></span></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-powershell"><span># 1) Clear out the bogus build command &amp; set publish dir to “.” via the Netlify API
netlify api updateSite --data '{\"site_id\":\"same-k9b4q7zbb4s-latest\",\"build_settings\":{\"cmd\":\"\",\"dir\":\".\"}}'

# 2) Link this folder to your existing Netlify site (non‑interactive)
netlify init --manual --site same-k9b4q7zbb4s-latest --dir . --branch main

# 3) Do a one‑shot production deploy
netlify deploy --prod --dir . --site same-k9b4q7zbb4s-latest
</span></code></div></div></pre>
<p data-start="606" data-end="616"><strong data-start="606" data-end="616">Notes:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="618" data-end="1043">
<li data-start="618" data-end="778">
<p data-start="620" data-end="778">The first line uses the <code data-start="644" data-end="657">netlify api</code> command (it directly calls Netlify’s API) to <strong data-start="703" data-end="716">blank out</strong> any build command and ensure your publish directory is <code data-start="772" data-end="775">.</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="779" data-end="966">
<p data-start="781" data-end="966">The second line uses <code data-start="802" data-end="825">netlify init --manual</code> (not <code data-start="831" data-end="842">--site-id</code>) to link your local folder to the site with ID <code data-start="890" data-end="915">same-k9b4q7zbb4s-latest</code>, and tells it that your deploy branch is <code data-start="957" data-end="963">main</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="967" data-end="1043">
<p data-start="969" data-end="1043">The third line pushes your current folder up as a <strong data-start="1019" data-end="1033">production</strong> deploy.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1045" data-end="1100">Once that runs successfully, future updates are simply:</p>
