git add assets/.gitkeep
git commit -m </span><span><span class="hljs-string">"Create assets folder with placeholder"</span></span><span>
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="836" data-end="1013">Once your <code data-start="846" data-end="855">assets/</code> folder is in place with the real image files, everything will resolve correctly. Then push to GitHub and Netlify will pick up your assets on the next deploy.</p>
